course: dictionary
lesson: 9644
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary gives each meaning its own number, so you choose the right one by reading the sentence around the word. This is the same context detective work you used for famished and curt.
explain: «Sturgeons are ancient fish that have changed little since the age of dinosaurs» uses sturgeon for an animal: it swims, lives in water and has changed little over millions of years. The dictionary calls this meaning 1).
explain: Sturgeon can also mean the meat of the fish, eaten as food. Look for clues such as cooking, menus or eggs. Then swap your meaning into the sentence: «The sturgeon swam up the river» only makes sense with the fish meaning.
fact: A sturgeon is a very large, old kind of fish with a long nose.
fact: Sturgeons have rows of bony plates instead of normal scales.
fact: Sturgeons live in rivers and seas of the northern part of the world.
fact: «Sturgeon» can also mean the meat of the fish, eaten as food.
fact: The eggs of a sturgeon are made into caviar.
exercise: «A sturgeon has five rows of bony plates along its body and four whiskers under its snout.» What does the sturgeon have instead of normal scales? | Feathers | *Bony plates | Fur | Shells
exercise: «Ancient sturgeons with bony plates swim up the Danube.» What does ancient mean? | Very fast | Very small | *Very old | Brand new
exercise: On a menu, you read «Smoked sturgeon with lemon». Which meaning of sturgeon is this? | *The meat of the fish, eaten as food | A fish swimming in a river | A kind of bony plate | A river in the north
test: Sturgeons have existed since the time of the dinosaurs. What kind of animal is a sturgeon? | Mammal | Reptile | Bird | *Fish
test: «The beluga sturgeon can live over 100 years and grow longer than a car.» What does this sentence tell you? | Cars are made from fish | Sturgeons cannot grow at all | Sturgeons are small and short-lived | *Some sturgeons live very long and grow very large
exam: «Chinese sturgeon live in the sea and swim up the Yangtze to lay eggs.» Which meaning of sturgeon fits, and why? | *The fish, because the sentence says they swim and lay eggs | The bony plates, because they are on the body | The meat, because it is cooked in the sea | A river in China, because the Yangtze is a river
